Text-to-image diffusion models<|CIT-MASK|> have achieved remarkable success in generating realistic high-resolution images. Building on this foundation, techniques for personalizing these models have also advanced. Various methods for single-concept customization<|CIT-MASK|> have been proposed, enabling the generation of images of the target concept in specified contexts based on user-provided visual conditions. These methods allow users to place real-world subjects into imagined scenes, greatly enriching the application scenarios of image generation.

